<item>
<title><![CDATA[Apple wants to save money on the iPhone 18 Pro Max's screen]]></title>
<link>https://www.gsmarena.com/apple_wants_to_save_money_on_the_iphone_18_pro_maxs_screen-news-73877.php</link>
<guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.gsmarena.com/apple_wants_to_save_money_on_the_iphone_18_pro_maxs_screen-news-73877.php</guid>
<pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 23:59:02 +0200</pubDate>
<description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://fdn.gsmarena.com/imgroot/news/26/07/iphone-18-pro-max-cheaper-screen/-184x111/gsmarena_000.jpg&quot; width=&quot;184&quot; height=&quot;111&quot; hspace=&quot;3&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot; align=left style="background:#333333;padding:0px;margin:0px 4px 0px 0px;border-style:solid;border-color:#aaaaaa;border-width:1px" /&gt; &lt;p&gt;<![CDATA[According to a new rumor out of Korea, Apple is trying to offset some of the higher costs of memory and storage for its upcoming iPhone 18 Pro Max by getting cheaper displays.

In fact, its panel suppliers Samsung Display and LG are apparently selling Apple the iPhone 18 Pro Max's screen at an average price of $66.5, which is allegedly almost 20% below what Apple paid for the iPhone 17 Pro Max's screen last year (in the $80 range).



Even last year, Apple was getting cheaper displays than the year before that, with the iPhone 16 Pro Max's screen reportedly costing above $100 at times....]]>&lt;/p&gt;</description>
<comments>https://www.gsmarena.com/newscomm-73877.php</comments>
<category>news</category>
</item>

	

	

<item>
<title><![CDATA[Samsung Galaxy S25 series could get One UI 9 beta soon]]></title>
<link>https://www.gsmarena.com/samsung_galaxy_s25_series_one_ui_9_beta_release_soon-news-73883.php</link>
<guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.gsmarena.com/samsung_galaxy_s25_series_one_ui_9_beta_release_soon-news-73883.php</guid>
<pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 20:51:02 +0200</pubDate>
<description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://fdn.gsmarena.com/imgroot/news/25/09/samsung-galaxy-s25-ultra-one-ui-8-5-test-build/-184x111/gsmarena_001.jpg&quot; width=&quot;184&quot; height=&quot;111&quot; hspace=&quot;3&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot; align=left style="background:#333333;padding:0px;margin:0px 4px 0px 0px;border-style:solid;border-color:#aaaaaa;border-width:1px" /&gt; &lt;p&gt;<![CDATA[Samsung is internally testing Android 17-based One UI 9 for several Galaxy devices, including the Galaxy S25 series; however, the Korean company has released One UI 9 beta only for the Galaxy S26 lineup so far. Well, the good news is the Galaxy S25 series could receive One UI 9 beta soon.

The first One UI 9 beta build for the Galaxy S25 Ultra has been spotted on Samsung's server with firmware versions S938NKSUBZZG8/S938NOKRBZZG8/S938NKSUBDZG8. However, note that the build is for the S25 Ultra's Korean model, so expect the One UI 9 beta to release in South Korea first, then expand to other...]]>&lt;/p&gt;</description>
<comments>https://www.gsmarena.com/newscomm-73883.php</comments>
<category>news</category>
</item>

	

	

<item>
