<pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 03:02:02 +0200</pubDate>
<description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://fdn.gsmarena.com/imgroot/news/26/07/samsung-galaxy-f70-pro-key-specs-geekbench/-184x111/gsmarena_001.jpg&quot; width=&quot;184&quot; height=&quot;111&quot; hspace=&quot;3&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot; align=left style="background:#333333;padding:0px;margin:0px 4px 0px 0px;border-style:solid;border-color:#aaaaaa;border-width:1px" /&gt; &lt;p&gt;<![CDATA[Samsung unveiled the Galaxy F70e in February, and we might see it launch a Pro model in the coming months, as the smartphone was spotted on the GSMA database a few months ago and has now popped up on Geekbench.

The benchmark database reveals that the Samsung Galaxy F70 Pro, bearing model code SM-E476B, is powered by Qualcomm's SM6475 chip, which corresponds to the Snapdragon 6 Gen 3 SoC. It consists of two quad-core clusters - one having a maximum clock speed of 1.8GHz and the other having a clock speed of up to 2.4GHz. GPU is likely Adreno 710.



Samsung Galaxy F70e

