<item>
<title><![CDATA[Facebook Verified is a new free badge that confirms there's a real person behind an account]]></title>
<link>https://www.gsmarena.com/facebook_verified_is_a_new_free_badge_that_confirms_theres_a_real_person_behind_an_account-news-73876.php</link>
<guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.gsmarena.com/facebook_verified_is_a_new_free_badge_that_confirms_theres_a_real_person_behind_an_account-news-73876.php</guid>
<pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 23:03:02 +0200</pubDate>
<description>&lt;img src=&quot;https://fdn.gsmarena.com/imgroot/news/26/07/facebook-verified-badge/-184x111/gsmarena_000.jpg&quot; width=&quot;184&quot; height=&quot;111&quot; hspace=&quot;3&quot; alt=&quot;&quot; border=&quot;0&quot; align=left style="background:#333333;padding:0px;margin:0px 4px 0px 0px;border-style:solid;border-color:#aaaaaa;border-width:1px" /&gt; &lt;p&gt;<![CDATA[Today Meta is launching Facebook Verified. This is a free badge that lets you know there's a real person behind an account. To get the badge, you need to go through a selfie-based verification process. You basically record a selfie video, which the company will check against your existing profile pictures to confirm a match. The process should only take a few minutes.

If you get the badge, it will initially appear in Facebook Marketplace, Dating, Groups, and on your profile. In the future, it will also be seen in Feed posts. Obviously, the badge doesn't mean that Facebook "endorses the...]]>&lt;/p&gt;</description>
<comments>https://www.gsmarena.com/newscomm-73876.php</comments>
<category>news</category>
</item>

	

	

<item>
